      "writtenOn": "2023-10-04T01:48:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be unnecessary or even undesirable to have `mFileEntries` (a consumable enumeration of the entries inside the zip file) be a instance member. It\u0027s only really \"used\" in this function and it seems that in the \"happy path\" (no invalid compression method used), `mFilesEntries.hasMoreElements() \u003d\u003d false` by the end of this function. If there\u0027s no intention to use it elsewhere, making it a instance member might be error prone.\n\nPerhaps keep it local to this function. Example:\n\n```java\nEnumeration\u003cZipEntry\u003e fileEntries \u003d mUpdateZipFile.entries();\nwhile (fileEntries.hasMoreElements) {\n  ZipEntry entry \u003d fileEntries.nextElement();\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nOn a larger note, it seems like `clearPayloadMetadata()` is only ever called right before `updatePayloadMetadata()`. Maybe just make it one function `parsePayloadMetadata(String updateFilePath)` that just resets / re-parses the zip file? A bonus is that updateFilePath does not need to be an instance member either.",
